<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31634" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑκᾰτόμ-βοιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ʽβοῦσ̓</span>”
				<i>worth a hundred oxen,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.449
				</span></i>
			, etc.: expld. as <i>worth</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				100
			</span></i>
			<i>pieces of money,</i> the ancient coins being stamped with an
			ox, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				252.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				320.47
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑκατόμβοια</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερά</span>), τά,
				<i>festival at which hecatombs were offered</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				36.36
			</span></i> (Delph., V B.C.), <i><span class="en">
				82.6
			</span></i> (Delph., V B.C.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>BCH</u>
				29.243
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Delos</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(2).142
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Tegea</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				8.4.11
			</span></i> codd.: dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑκατομβούοις</span>
			(sic) <i><span class="en">
				<u>Schwyzer</u>
				91.19
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Argos</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
